# Odoo MCP

The `odoo` MCP server talks to the **production** Odoo.sh database (instance
`odoosh`). Treat every call as touching live customer data.

- Before guessing a schema, call `get_model_fields` (use `relevance="top"` on
  wide models) or `inspect_model_relationships`.
- Prefer `search_records` with an explicit `fields` list; use
  `aggregate_records` for counts and sums instead of reading rows.
- Never call `create`/`write`/`unlink` through `execute_method`. Writes go
  through `preview_write` → `validate_write` → `execute_approved_write`, and
  only when the user has asked for the change in this conversation.
- On a permission error, pass the error text to `diagnose_access` as
  `observed_error` instead of retrying.
- If more than one instance is configured, run `list_instances` and pass
  `instance` explicitly on every call.
